            <ArticleTitle>Giant Orf on the Nose.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/SCS.0000000000003441</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Orf is a zoonotic infectious disease caused by parapoxvirus. Orf lesions are typically seen on the hand, but they have rarely been reported on the nose. Herein, the authors report a rare patient of an orf lesion on the nose of a 52-year-old man after the Muslim celebration of the feast of the sacrifice. The lesion spontaneously recovered 8 weeks after the initial appearance and showed no evidence of recurrence after 1 year of follow-up. Orf virus infections may occur more often after the celebration of the feast of the sacrifice in Muslim countries.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
